# Exclude development-only files from the published registry archive.
# .comfyignore layers on top of .gitignore, so anything already
# gitignored is excluded automatically. This drops files we keep in git
# but do not want inside the registry package.

# A leading slash anchors a pattern to the repository root. These are
# gitignore-style patterns, so an unanchored `tests/` would also match a
# `js/tests/` added later -- and an unanchored `previews/` below would
# match `js/previews/`, shipping a registry package whose style gallery
# has no thumbnails at all. `node_modules/` stays unanchored on purpose:
# a nested one is still node_modules.
/tests/
/scripts/
/examples/
/user_styles.example.json
/package.json
/package-lock.json
node_modules/

# Repository scaffolding. None of it is read at runtime and none of it is
# linked from the README, so it is pure weight in a registry install.
# ARCHITECTURE.md and docs/custom-styles.md are NOT here: the README links
# both, and a dead link on the registry page is worse than the bytes.
/.github/
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
/.gitattributes
/.nojekyll

# The preview build ledger: content hashes read only by
# scripts/build_previews.py, which is itself excluded above. The atlases
# the gallery actually draws from live in js/previews/ and stay -- hence
# the leading slash, which is what keeps this from matching them too.
/previews/

# docs/ is NOT excluded wholesale: docs/images is what the README links
# to. docs/worklog is gitignored, so it never reaches the package anyway.
#
# docs/gallery IS excluded. It is the public web gallery, generated for
# GitHub Pages, and it is nearly 400 KB of duplicated style text that a
# ComfyUI install has no use for -- the in-app picker reads the same data
# from js/stylebook_data.js.
/docs/gallery/

# docs/reference is excluded for the same reason: generated web-only
# reference pages served by GitHub Pages, of no use in an install.
/docs/reference/

# js/previews/ is deliberately NOT excluded. Those atlases are what the
# style gallery draws its thumbnails from, so a registry install without
# them would open an empty gallery. They total about 4 MB and keep the
# pack working fully offline, with no download on first use.
